1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,925
The Deep Ocean.

2
00:00:01,875 --> 00:00:12,937
The deep ocean begins at 200 meters, where sunlight diminishes below the level required for photosynthesis, and extends to approximately 11,000 meters in the Mariana Trench.

3
00:00:12,937 --> 00:00:23,087
This region constitutes 95 percent of Earth's habitable volume by biosphere, yet less than 25 percent of the seafloor has been mapped to modern bathymetric standards.

4
00:00:23,087 --> 00:00:29,700
As of 2026, only 2 percent of the deep ocean has been directly observed by human exploration.

5
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:40,412
Pressure increases by one atmosphere every 10 meters, reaching approximately 1,100 atmospheres (110 megapascals) in the deepest trenches.

6
00:00:40,412 --> 00:00:44,525
Deep-sea organisms have evolved extraordinary adaptations.

7
00:00:44,525 --> 00:00:54,675
The barophilic enzymes of hadal fish function only under extreme pressure; cellular membranes incorporate high proportions of unsaturated fatty acids to maintain fluidity.

8
00:00:54,675 --> 00:01:04,812
Many species exhibit deep-sea gigantism — the giant amphipod Alicella gigantea reaches 34 centimeters, five times the length of shallow-water relatives.

9
00:01:04,812 --> 00:01:16,362
Bioluminescence, produced by luciferin-luciferase reactions, is used by over 80 percent of deep-sea species for counter-illumination camouflage, prey attraction, and mate signaling.

10
00:01:16,362 --> 00:01:30,662
Hydrothermal vents, discovered in 1977 along the Galapagos Rift by the submersible Alvin, discharge fluids at temperatures up to 407 degrees Celsius, rich in hydrogen sulfide, methane, and dissolved metals.

11
00:01:30,662 --> 00:01:40,462
These fluids support chemosynthetic bacteria and archaea that oxidize reduced inorganic compounds to fix carbon, forming a food web independent of sunlight.

12
00:01:40,462 --> 00:01:54,837
Giant tube worms (Riftia pachyptila) lack digestive systems entirely, relying on symbiotic sulfide-oxidizing bacteria within a specialized organ called the trophosome, achieving growth rates of 85 centimeters per year.

13
00:01:54,837 --> 00:02:00,450
Vent fields remain active for decades to centuries before tectonic shifts extinguish them.

14
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:15,187
Exploration milestones include James Cameron's 2012 solo dive to 10,908 meters in the Mariana Trench and the Five Deeps Expedition (2018-2019), which sent manned submersibles to all five ocean trenches.

15
00:02:15,187 --> 00:02:21,750
Despite these advances, NOAA estimates 91 percent of marine species remain undescribed.

